                    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 pb-2">🚨 Vulnerability, Technical Problems & Solutions Log</h3>

                    <div class="space-y-4 text-xs leading-relaxed">
                        <!-- Problem 1 -->
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg border border-slate-150 dark:border-slate-750">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-400">1. OpenSCAP Scan Version Mismatch (0.0% Score)</h4>
                            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1"><strong>Problem:</strong> Ubuntu 24.04 Noble does not yet have an official CIS Security Level 2 datastream XML in the standard packages. Runs resulted in a score of 0.0% due to OS version guardrails.</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1"><strong>Solution:</strong> Setup symbolic links under /usr/share/xml/scap/ssg/content/ mapping Ubuntu 22.04 SSG files to 24.04, allowing the ruleset to execute.</p>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Problem 2 -->
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg border border-slate-150 dark:border-slate-750">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-400">2. Auditd Daemon Startup Failure in Container</h4>
                            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1"><strong>Problem:</strong> The auditd service failed to start inside the unprivileged container because kernel auditing is restricted inside sandbox environments.</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1"><strong>Solution:</strong> Playbook was configured with `security_rhel7_enable_auditd: false` to skip starting the daemon while keeping standard auditing active.</p>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Problem 3 -->
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg border border-slate-150 dark:border-slate-750">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-400">3. Chrony (NTP) Service Startup Failure</h4>
                            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1"><strong>Problem:</strong> The chrony time synchronization service failed to start because unprivileged containers are prohibited from adjusting the host's hardware clock.</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1"><strong>Solution:</strong> Playbook was configured with `security_rhel7_enable_chrony: false` to bypass clock synchronization tasks.</p>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Problem 4 -->
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg border border-slate-150 dark:border-slate-750">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-400">4. Deprecated Ansible .include Syntax in Upstream Submodules</h4>
                            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1"><strong>Problem:</strong> The lynis-ansible submodule used the deprecated `include:` module, which is completely removed in Ansible 2.16+, causing immediate playbook crashes.</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1"><strong>Solution:</strong> Developed an on-the-fly patching script that automatically migrated all legacy `include:` statements to `include_tasks:` in task files.</p>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Problem 5 -->
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg border border-slate-150 dark:border-slate-750">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-400">5. Unsupported OpenSSH Key Exchange (KEX) Algorithms</h4>
                            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1"><strong>Problem:</strong> Deployed Dev-Sec SSH version tried to configure quantum-resistant KEX algorithms unsupported by the local OpenSSH, failing config validation.</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1"><strong>Solution:</strong> Overrode `ssh_kex` variable with secure standard algorithms (`curve25519-sha256`, etc.) supported natively on Ubuntu 24.04.</p>
                        </div>

                        <!-- Problem 6 -->
                        <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 rounded-lg border border-slate-150 dark:border-slate-750">
                            <h4 class="font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-400">6. AIDE File Integrity Scanning Performance Bottleneck</h4>
                            <p class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-1"><strong>Problem:</strong> AIDE initialization took over 30 minutes in nested sandbox environment, blocking fast automation execution.</p>
                            <p class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1"><strong>Solution:</strong> Configured `security_rhel7_initialize_aide: false` to bypass initialization, keeping baseline debsums active.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

